<H1>Motorcycle Trip to Bend, Oregon April 28, 2021</H1>
<BR>
<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=105IXx_s4bIevVnnMP-uILSlxmtLjmmNF" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_bend_20210428.jpg" ALIGN=RIGHT style="width:592px"></A>
A playlist of all of <a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL65CwO7O2fX8mpc9xT7Ppuukulf934tj9" target="_blank">the videos from</A> the ride from April 28 thru May 01, 2021.
<BR><BR>
You can easily ride just the Interstates down to Bend Oregon, or you can make it more interesting. My <A HREF="https://butlermaps.com/" target="_blank">Butler Maps</a> helped immensely in picking out alternative routes that would give me some nice roads to ride. 
<BR><BR>
Crossed over <a href="https://youtu.be/VKUKFFp9p48" target="_blank">Snoqualamie Pass</A>, I-90. Mountains still has lots of snow on them.
<BR><BR>
Further on is <A HREF="https://stateparks.oregon.gov/index.cfm?do=park.profile&parkId=195" target="_blank">Cottonwood Canyon State Park</A> (Near The Dalles, Oregon). gorgeous mix of river and semi-arid desert:<BR>
<A HREF="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yisBhJcA5gYRt7Y4f1lSt68kGf1NYQfp/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_bend_20210428_1_cottonwood_canyon_sm.jpg"></A>
<BR><BR>
When you get to  <A HREF="https://www.google.com/maps/@45.3801846,-120.4014832,113m/data=!3m1!1e3" target="_blank">Highway 206</A> (about 200+ miles into this ride) you will see a little pulloff. From there you can (on a VERY clear day) see quite a few of the West Coast volcanoes :<BR>
<A HREF="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Cc8oT7QInMqrypLHxtkZ91iR6LfkgICQ/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_bend_20210428_2_Hwy_206_sm.jpg"></A>
<BR><BR>
A veiw of the West Coast volcanoes without the road sign:<BR>
<A HREF="https://drive.google.com/file/d/15qdCxrfsg8gDEpqpncxJqE10fUnDS8e_/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_bend_20210428_3_Hwy_206_sm.jpg"></A>
<BR><BR>
And a few miles down <a href="https://youtu.be/leNXqbD7S0I" target="_blank">Oregon Hwy19</A> South of Fossil OR has more twisties in store in the mountains and through the trees. The road was a little dicey so I tucked down for this ride which is why the camera is pointing a little low.
<BR><BR>
When we went out to dinner we noticed that Bend, OR has an ... Interesting ... aroma (from all the Juniper trees). <a href="https://www.bing.com/search?q=Bend%20Oregon%20Juniper%20smell" target="_blank">Some like it</A>, other people not so much.
<BR><BR>
From there off to lodgings in Bend, OR for the night.
<BR><BR>
